s, the interrupt can occur at any point during main execution, including between the read at line 7 and write at line 8 in `munge()`.\n\n## Summary of Analysis\n\nAll read/write operations on `myglobal` can be executed:\n- Lines 7-8 in `munge()` will execute when called from main\n- Lines 13-14 in `isr_munge()` will execute when the interrupt occurs\n- There are no control conditions preventing any of these operations\n- Interrupts are always enabled, allowing preemption\n\nThe atomicity violation reported in the initial defect is valid as the interrupt can preempt between the read at line 7 and write at line 8 in `munge()`, potentially causing a race condition with the write at line 14 in `isr_munge()`.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [7, 14, 8]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [7, 14, 8]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
